---
title: Beef with Coriander (Xiang Cai Niu Rou 香菜牛肉)
description: A very quick and flavorful stir-fry featuring tender beef slices heavily spiced with cumin and chili, tossed with fresh coriander and scallions.
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 5 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - beef
  - stir-fry
  - spicy
  - quick
  - chinese
image: https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/q_92,fl_progressive,w_1200,c_scale/v1/img/recipes/40/66/79/piccx65p8.jpg
cuisine: Chinese
course: Main
---

== Preparation ==

Prepare the @filet of beef{400%g} by hammering it with a meat cleaver or the side of a chinese meat cleaver to tenderize. Slice it into wafer thin slices.

In a bowl or plate, mix the spicy coating: @ground cumin{2%tbsp}, @dried chili pepper flakes{2%tbsp}, @ground black pepper{1%tbsp}, and @sea salt{1/2%tsp}. Coat the sliced beef thoroughly in this spice mix.

Roughly chop the @cilantro{50%g} (leaves and stalks) and finely chop the @scallion{1}.

== Cooking ==

Heat a #wok{} or pan over high heat and add the @peanut oil{2%tbsp}.

Add the coated beef and stir-fry for less than ~{1%minute} until browned and tender.

As the beef starts to cook, add the @rice wine{1%tsp} (or dry sherry) and season with the @soy sauce{1%tbsp} and an extra pinch of salt if desired.

== Finishing ==

Take the wok off the heat. Immediately stir in the chopped cilantro and scallion.

Serve immediately, optionally with steamed rice or warmed flatbreads.
